ns  C G  Lesion  lateral to medial  In the same container  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm unoriented fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm overlying skin is identified  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal fibrofatty cut surface with fat necrosis and no discrete lesions  Representative sections are submitted as H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary lymph node content  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm fibrofatty tissue containing multiple lymph nodes which are dissected  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm firm stellate fibrous area with tan gray solid cut surface  Lymph nodes are submitted as follows  I K  Multiple nodes  whole  L N  Fibrous stellate lesion  O Q  2 nodes per cassette  bisected  Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Yes.
