Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 31 CLINICAL DATA  FNA showed ductal carcinoma of right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT   REDUCTION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the mastectomy specimen appear free of the tumor  In the axillary lymph nodes  the metastatic foci take the form of isolated clusters of malignant cells that aggregate to less than 0 2cm in each node and do not transgress the lymph node capsules  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protien  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and 