              IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block B   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Right  block E   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 08     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block E   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   Breast  Right  block B   Insufficient tissue present for evaluation of HER 2 neu by FISH  See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm fibroadipose lumpectomy specimen oriented with a short suture superior  a long lateral and a double deep  The specimen is inked as follows  deep black  anterior blue  lateral green  medial yellow  Serial sectioning reveals two poorly defined  fibrous areas identified by two localization wires and clips  The superior fibrous area measures 0 8cm in diameter and shows contraction  It is located 1 5cm from the superior  1 5cm from the medial  4 0cm from the lateral  8 0cm from the inferior  0 4cm from the superficial and 1 0cm from the deep margin  The second radial fibrous area measures 1 5cm in diameter and is located 2 0cm from the lateral end medial  1 2cm from the inferior  6 5cm from the superior  0 3cm from the superficial and 1 5cm from the deep margin  The superior mass is located 1 0cm from the deep margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Superior mass in relationship to the superficial and lateral margins  B  Superior nodule in relationship to the deep margin  C  Superior nodule in relationship to the superficial and lateral margins  this area has been submitted entirely in cassettes A C  D  Inferior nodule  in relationship to the deep margin  full cross section  E G  Inferior mass in relationship to the inferior margin  H  Unremarkable adipose tissue adjacent  deeply to the inferior nodule  I  Unremarkable adipose tissue adjacent laterally to the inferior nodule  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  are two fatty soft tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm each  A lymph node is dissected from each  bisected and half of each is frozen as FX  1 2  now submitted in cassettes J K respectively  The remaining lymphoid tissue is submitted in cassette L  M and N  bivalved  and  O and ZZ separated   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  inferior  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 1 5cm specimen which is unoriented  The specimen is serially sectioned reveal focal areas of fibrosis but no definite masses  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes P Y  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  medial  right breast  is a fibroadipose specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The unoriented specimen is unoriented  serially sectioned and submitted in cassettes Z GG  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  lateral  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue specimen which is unoriented  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes HH NN  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shave margins  superior  right breast  are 3 fibroadipose tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes OO RR  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary lymph node  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm adipose tissue mass containing 5 lymph nodes submitted as follows  SS  1 lymph node bivalved  TT  2 lymph nodes bivalved  UU  Adiposee tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lymph node with minor amount of additional adipose tissue  The lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes VV WW  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO NODES  O R  Resident  NICOLE ANN BELSLEY  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  RE