Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  05 AUG 97 at 10 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  PHYLLODES TUMOR  29 0 CM   LOW GRADE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor displays  2 mitotic figures per 10 HPF  and lacks marked cellular pleomorphism  Stromal overgrowth is not seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with the diagnosis  2  ALL  12  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF TUMOR    LYMPH NODES   RIGHT AXILLA   ALL  5  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  1   SKIN WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  2   SKIN WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 18 06                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  are four parts  Labeled with patient s name only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 14 0cm mastectomy specimen with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 27 0cm ellipse of skin with an eccentrically placed 5 0cm nipple aveolar complex and a 14  x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  On external examination  a large multi nodular  tumor occupies the majority   95   of the specimen  the tumor does not grossly involve the deep margin  Cross sectioning of the mastectomy specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm  multi lobulated  well defined mass which compresses the normal surrounding breast tissue  The cut surface reveals numerous white whorled bulging  firm  rubbery lobulations  The lobulations range in diameter from 10 0cm to less than 0 2cm  In between the lobulations are cyst like and slit like spaces  the largest of which is 4 0cm in greatest length  and 0 3cm in width  The interface of the tumor with the surrounding breast parenchyma is grossly non infiltrative  No areas of hermorrhage or necrosis are seen  A representative section of the specimen is frozen as FX 1  and submitted as A  a section of the closest deep resection margin is submitted in B C  Representative sections from different areas of the tumor mass are submitted in D U  Sections taken from the cyst like area are submitted in H I  Representative sections of tumor interfacing with surrounding breast parenchyma in S T  A section containing a small comedo like area submitted in U  The surrounding breast parenchyma is sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  No additional masses are found  Representative sections of unremarkable breast parenchyma are submitted in V W  Section of the axillary tail reveals multiple  red  firm lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm  All lymph nodes are submitted in W through BB  Received in a separate container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name only is an REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm skin ellipse with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm adipose tissue  The surface of the skin ellipse and cut surface of the adipose tissue are unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in CC  Received in a separate container  labeled  lymph nodes  are three fragments of adipose tissue which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in total aggregate  The adipose tissue is dissected to reveal multiple  tan  firm lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  All submitted in DD through EE  Received in a separate container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number is an REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  unremarkable skin ellipse with attached underlying adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in greatest dimension  A representative section of skin is submitted in FF  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGN