tions with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 00     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Three specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  right breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen oriented by a short stitch superior and a long stitch lateral  with an overlying triangular  REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple areola complex  There are no scars in the overlying skin  However  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm erythematous area  with a palpable firmness 5 0cm inferior to the nipple  The excised surface is inked black  Cross sectioning reveals an ill defined firm  white REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nodule  located 2 0cm beneath the inferior portion of the skin  and coming to within 2 2cm of the nearest margin  deep   There is firm white fibrous tissue extending away from the nodule and a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of hemorrhage extending from this white fibrous tissue anterior to the overlying skin suggestive of a prior biopsy site  These changes are located beneath the erythematous nodule visible on the skin surface  Approximately 1 0cm anterior and medial to this lesion is a second very firm yellow tan  well demarcated nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which comes to within 1 8cm of the nearest margin  anterior skin   The remainder of the specimen consists of dense white fibrous tissue mixed with adipose tissue  Within the fibrous areas are scattered microcysts  The border of this white fibrous tissue averages 1 5cm from the deep margin  There is a third  firm  ill defined lesion  0 5cm in largest dimension  located in the inferior portion of the breast  1 6cm from the deep margin  Section code  A C  Firm white nodule described first D F  Previous biopsy site G H  Second nodule described  I L  Representative sections away from nodules  M  Suspicious area in medial portion of breast  greater than 2 0cm from the margins  N  Third nodule described  The attached axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  and is dissected for lymph nodes  which are submitted in O through R  Designated  right additional axillary node tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fatty tissue  containing several small lymph nodes  The lymph nodes are submitted in S  Designated  left breast  are multiple irregular fragments of breast tissue  some of them containing overlying skin  aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Cross sectioning reveals no discrete lesions  Representative sections are in T through CC  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA ADDITIONAL   EXCISION PART C  BREST  LEFT   MASTOPEXY , No.
