edial to lateral as follows  A  representative toward medial margin B  fibrous tissue to superior margin C  lesion to anterior inferior margin D  lesion to anterior and skin margin E  fibrous tissues to posterior margin F  fat necrosis to posterior inferior margin G  inked lesion to skin inferior margin H  lesion to anterior skin margin I J  full thickness section with the superior margin in I K  representative of fibrous to superior and inferior margins Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan red rubbery fatty lymph node with which is bisected and entirely submitted as L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary nonsentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan red rubbery fatty lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted as M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a 90  yellow lobulated fatty to 10  dense white fibrous tissue  Specimen is entirely submitted as N O  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast final lateral margin  are two portions of fibrofatty breast tissue averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm which are bisected to reveal a 70  yellow fatty lobulated fatty to 30  dense white fibrous tissue  Specimen is entirely submitted as P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast final stage inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments which are bisected to reveal a predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue surface  Specimen is entirely submitted as Q R  Received in formalin   l